/target
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock IS tracked: this workspace builds deployed wasm binaries (an app),
# so pinning deps keeps CI reproducible — an unpinned wasm-bindgen drifted to a
# newer glue form than local and broke the Firefox patch in CI.
bin/
# wasm-pack output: ignore the generated .wasm/.js/package.json, but TRACK the
# high-level `game_of_life_gpu.d.ts` — the public TypeScript API surface — so a
# #[wasm_bindgen] change shows up in the commit diff (audit Part 1 #1). NB:
# ignoring `pkg/` (the dir) made the old `!*.d.ts` negation dead (git can't
# re-include a file under an ignored dir), so we ignore the CONTENTS (`pkg/*`).
# The `*_bg.wasm.d.ts` glue typings are RE-ignored: they carry version-specific
# mangled wasm-bindgen symbol names that churn on every toolchain bump and are
# not a real API surface.
crates/*/pkg/*
!crates/*/pkg/*.d.ts
crates/*/pkg/*_bg.wasm.d.ts
wasm-pack.log
app/node_modules/
app/dist/
app/.tests-dist/
docs/*
.DS_Store
.claude
engineering-codex
CLAUDE.md